# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The one file in this repo that can do real damage is `.env`: it holds SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY,
# which BYPASSES row-level security and can write to or wipe the price database. A leaked
# service_role key is not a password reset — it is a full-access credential that has to be
# rotated in Supabase before anything else is done.
#
# So the rule is deny-by-default: every `.env*` variant is ignored, and only the committed
# template is allowed back. Adding `.env.production` later then cannot leak by being a
# filename nobody thought to list.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Anything that looks like a key, certificate or exported credential. None of these exist in
# the repo today — they are here so that a future one cannot be committed by accident.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets.json
secrets.*.json
credentials.json
*credentials*.json
service-account*.json
*.private
id_rsa*

# Generated by desktop/build.ps1: a copy of the Supabase credentials from .env, written so
# PyInstaller can bake them into the .exe and deleted again the moment the build ends. It
# should never be present when you commit — this line is here in case a build was killed.
desktop/_baked.py

# ── Commercially sensitive data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This repository is PUBLIC, and these two files are IMECO's pricing strategy in plain form:
# every SKU, its MRP, the intended selling price per marketplace, and every listing URL. None
# of it is a credential, so nothing breaks if it leaks — it is simply the sort of thing a
# competitor would rather not be handed.
#
# The app does not need them to be in git. `Docs/pricing link.example.xlsx` IS committed and
# documents the exact column contract; the operator supplies the real sheet through the
# desktop app's Spreadsheet button, which stores it in %LOCALAPPDATA%.
Docs/pricing link.xlsx
public/demo-prices.json
!Docs/pricing link.example.xlsx

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything here is regenerated by `npm run build` or `desktop/build.ps1`. Committing it
# means every rebuild shows up as a diff of unreadable bundled bytes.
#
# A bare `dist/` already matches a directory of that name at ANY depth. The explicit paths
# below are for the reader, not for git — the .exe in particular is 16 MB and would otherwise
# be a surprise in someone's clone.
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
desktop/dist/
desktop/build/
*.local

# The single-file .exe, wherever it is built or copied to. It is handed to staff directly,
# not distributed through git.
*.exe

# ── Node / Vite ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# PyInstaller scratch: the throwaway build venv, its work directory, and the spec file it
# regenerates on every run. See desktop/build.ps1 for why the venv exists.
desktop/.buildenv/
*.spec

# Local runtime state, not source. `desktop/.state/budget.json` is this machine's Bright Data
# credit counter — committing it would hand another machine a used-up allowance.
desktop/.state/

# ── Deployment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel/
.netlify/

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Excel's lock file, written whenever the workbook is open. The workbook itself IS committed —
# the app bundles it — but this temporary sibling must not be.
~$*.xlsx

# ── Claude Code ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
